== About

I am Assoc. Prof. Vo Thi Luu Phuong (published as *Phuong Luu Vo*), an Associate Professor at the
School of Computer Science and Engineering, International University -- Vietnam National
University Ho Chi Minh City, where I lead the *Network Optimization and Distributed Learning*
group.

I received my Ph.D. in Computer Engineering from Kyung Hee University, Korea, and have since
worked on the algorithms behind networked systems: how resources are shared, where content is
placed and how it is delivered, and -- more recently -- how learning can make those decisions
without a full model of the system. The questions the group is working on now are on the
[interests.html Research Interests] page.

=== Academic and professional appointments

- *Associate Professor*, School of Computer Science and Engineering, International University
  (VNU-HCM), currently.
- *Head of the IT Department*, School of Computer Science and Engineering, International
  University (VNU-HCM).
- *Researcher*, School of Computer Science and Engineering, International University (VNU-HCM),
  2007 to present.
- *Industry positions*, 1998--2007.

=== Education

- *Ph.D.* in Computer Engineering, Kyung Hee University, Seoul, Korea, 2009--2014.
- *M.Sc.* in Telecommunication, Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology, Vietnam, 1999--2003.

